  m_Name: About_Us
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ArticlePageData
  title: About Us
  bodyText: "New Manila City Dog Shelter\r\n\r\nThe New Manila City Dog Shelter is
    the official municipal animal control and care facility operating under the Office
    of the City Veterinarian (pursuant to Municipal Ordinance No. 204). The shelter
    protects public health, enforces animal welfare standards, and provides shelter,
    medical treatment, and rehoming services for stray, lost, and surrendered animals.\r\n\r\nMission
    Statement\r\nTo maintain a safe, humane municipal shelter system that safeguards
    public health, enforces local animal welfare regulations, and maximizes the placement
    of healthy animals into permanent homes.\r\n\r\nCore Services & Operations\r\n\r\nVeterinary
    & Shelter Care: Medical screenings, vaccinations, spay/neuter procedures, and
    daily rehabilitation.\r\n\r\nAdoption & Rehoming: Matching behaviorally assessed
    animals with qualified city residents.\r\n\r\nPublic Health & Safety: Managing
    stray populations, rabies prevention, and pet licensing enforcement.\r\n\r\n\r\nCitizen
    Participation\r\n\r\nAdopt: Browse eligible dogs via the municipal web portal
    or during scheduled public viewing hours.\r\n\r\nVolunteer: Apply for the Municipal
    Volunteer Corps to assist with daily dog care, walking, and outreach.\r\n\r\nFoster:
    Provide temporary home shelter for young puppies or animals undergoing medical
    recovery.\r\n\r\nFacility Directory & Hours\r\n\r\nLocation: Municipal Services
    Compound, Sector 4, New Manila City\r\n\r\nPublic Viewing Hours: Tuesday \u2013
    Sunday: 9:00 AM \u2013 4:00 PM (Closed Mondays)\r\n\r\nAdministrative Hours:
    Monday \u2013 Friday: 8:00 AM \u2013 5:00 PM\r\n\r\nContact: dogshelter@newmanila.gov.ph
    | (02) 8912-3456"
  images: []
